# Two fixed hosts, one process each (spec 2026-10-19-path-tenancy-design.md). The tenant is the first
# path segment (`/<slug>/…`), which each process reads from its SPA's calls — Caddy routes on the host
# only, so there is no wildcard name, no wildcard certificate and no DNS challenge.
#   app.{$DOMAIN}       sign-in, the /login dispatcher, and the staff app  -> server:3000
#   portal.{$DOMAIN}    the customer portal                                 -> portal:3001
#   {$DOMAIN}           nothing of its own yet                              -> sign-in
# The session cookie is on {$DOMAIN}, so every host under it receives it: never point a name under
# {$DOMAIN} at a service this stack does not control.
# ponytail: the apex only redirects until a marketing site exists; then serve that there instead.
#
# CADDY_TLS picks where certificates come from (compose defaults it to `internal`):
#   internal    Caddy's local CA, for running the full stack on lvh.me.
#   acme        Caddy's automatic HTTPS: one Let's Encrypt certificate per name, HTTP challenge on :80.
(tls-internal) {
	tls internal
}

(tls-acme) {
	tls {
		issuer acme
	}
}

app.{$DOMAIN} {
	import tls-{$CADDY_TLS}
	reverse_proxy server:3000
}

portal.{$DOMAIN} {
	import tls-{$CADDY_TLS}
	reverse_proxy portal:3001
}

{$DOMAIN} {
	import tls-{$CADDY_TLS}
	redir https://app.{$DOMAIN}/login
}
